            "review_title": "Review at Mojo Café & Bistro",
            "review_text": "Inlovewiththeworld\n3979 contributions\n0\nAn oasis of calm and elegance from the busy Walking Street outside.\nJan 2023 • Solo\nThis is an oasis of calm away from the noise and chaos of the Walking Street outside.  Elegant and like walking into another world.  Never very busy.  Easy to miss.  Located right next to McDonald's.  Big space.  Light and airy with lovely seating.  Think afternoon tea type of place or ladies that lunch!  Having said this, they serve breakfast all day, plus savoury items, desserts and more.  This is a good place for cakes, speciality drinks and coffees as well as smoothies and juices.  Instagram lovers will have a ball.  Most guests are expats, business colleagues, wealthy Vietnamese or foreigners.  Not too pricey.  My hotel was located nearby and I needed a break from the chain coffee shops!  The iced americano was so good.  One of the best I had with like a nutty taste.  It wasn't too bitter either.  So refreshing.  Well presented in a smaller glass that I liked as most places give massive glasses of iced coffee which is too much.  I went back a few times after as I enjoyed the peace, ambience and light music.  So cosy and comfortable.  Wifi was fast.  Staff were pleasant and generally friendly.  English was limited.  Service was a bit slow sometimes as the design of the premises was long with different seating areas.  Not sure if there was an upstairs too.  There were stairs!  Most of the staff would congregate near the back by the counter and till.  I would normally sit by the front door so it was difficult to always attract their attention.  Having said this, they were always quick to come and very nice.  What I loved was that they would let you relax in peace.  I would often sit for a few hours!  I ate once too.  Light starter which was very nice.  Simple but hit the spot.  Very fresh.  I was craving smoked salmon.  Savoury food includes salads, Vietnamese dishes and more.  My small negative was despite the premises being very clean most of the time, there was a hair once on my seat which put me off a bit and sometimes tables and floors were left dirty.  They had enough staff and were never very busy the many times I went.  Would recommend otherwise. \nRead more\nWritten January 15, 2023",
